%U A399778 161488849716213858611028268957330825564125,5323044123932949605736519659522967645144662861953125,572042539557508080505186333411453546901023071826325584164740625
%N A399778 Diagonal product divided by the central-cross sum in the (2*n + 1) X (2*n + 1) square array formed by the integers 1, 2, ..., (2*n + 1)^2 in order.
%C A399778 The array is formed by the integers 1, 2, ..., (2*n + 1)^2, arranged from left to right and from bottom to top. The central-cross sum is the sum of the entries in the central row and column, while the diagonal product is the product of the entries on the two main diagonals; in both cases, the common central entry is included only once.
%C A399778 For n = 1, the corresponding ratio is 945/25 = 189/5, which is not an integer; for every n >= 2, the ratio is an integer. Indeed, let c := 2*n^2 + 2*n + 1, so the central-cross sum is c*(4*n + 1) and the diagonal product is c*Product_{k = 1..n}((c^2 - 4*n^2*k^2)*(c^2 - 4*(n + 1)^2*k^2)). For n >= 2, the factor c^2 - 4*n^2*k^2 corresponding to k = n - 1 satisfies c^2 - 4*n^2*(n - 1)^2 = (4*n + 1)*(4*n^2 + 1), proving that the ratio is an integer.
%H A399778 Paolo Xausa, <a href="/A399778/b399778.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 2..65</a>
%H A399778 Wikipedia, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Calculator">Calculator (Key layout)</a>.
%F A399778 a(n) = (Product_{k = 1..n} (c^2 - 4*n^2*k^2)*(c^2 - 4*(n + 1)^2*k^2))/(4*n + 1) where c = 2*n^2 + 2*n + 1.
%F A399778 Limit_{n->infinity} a(n)^(1/n)/n^8 = 256/e^4.
%e A399778 For n = 2, the calculator array is
%e A399778   21 22 23 24 25
%e A399778   16 17 18 19 20
%e A399778   11 12 13 14 15
%e A399778    6  7  8  9 10
%e A399778    1  2  3  4  5.
%e A399778 The central-cross sum is 3 + 8 + 11 + 12 + 13 + 14 + 15 + 18 + 23 = 117, while the diagonal product is 1*5*7*9*13*17*19*21*25 = 694409625.
%e A399778 Hence, a(2) = 694409625/117 = 5935125.
%t A399778 A399778[n_] := Product[(# - 4*n^2*k^2)*(# - 4*(n + 1)^2*k^2), {k, n}]/(4*n + 1) & [(2*n*(n + 1) + 1)^2];
%t A399778 Array[A399778, 10, 2] (* _Paolo Xausa_, Oct 02 2026 *)
